<section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl" data-sw-animation="fade-up">
    <p class="ws-index ws-ink">05 · Wheel and auto height</p>
    <h2 class="ws-display mt-3 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-5xl" data-sw-text="c5_title">Slides of different heights.</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-base-content/70" data-sw-text="c5_lead">Scroll the mouse wheel or a trackpad over this one to move it. The track animates its height to fit each answer. It also opts out of looping, so the arrows dim at the first and the last slide, and it asks for the round arrow style.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-start">
<!--demo:wheel-->
<div class="relative" data-sw-component="carousel" data-sw-block="Carousel" data-effect="slide" data-wheel="true" data-autoheight="true" data-loop="false" data-arrows="circle" aria-label="Questions about the carousel">
  <div data-sw-part="track">
    <figure data-sw-part="slide" class="px-1 pb-12">
      <div class="rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-8 px-14">
        <p class="font-heading text-lg font-bold">Does it work without JavaScript?</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-base-content/70">Yes. The track is a CSS scroll-snap row, so it still swipes and scrolls. Arrows and dots stay hidden, so no dead controls show.</p>
      </div>
    </figure>
    <figure data-sw-part="slide" class="px-1 pb-12">
      <div class="rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-8 px-14">
        <p class="font-heading text-lg font-bold">Which library runs it?</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-base-content/70">Embla. It ships with the page only when the page contains a carousel.</p>
      </div>
    </figure>
    <figure data-sw-part="slide" class="px-1 pb-12">
      <div class="rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-8 px-14">
        <p class="font-heading text-lg font-bold">What does it do for screen readers?</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-base-content/70">The runtime adds a region role, the carousel role description and a hidden live region that announces the active slide. It stays silent while the carousel rotates on its own. Keep an <code class="font-code">aria-label</code> on the root.</p>
      </div>
    </figure>
    <figure data-sw-part="slide" class="px-1 pb-12">
      <div class="rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-8 px-14">
        <p class="font-heading text-lg font-bold">How do I space the cards?</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-base-content/70">With padding inside each slide. Slide margins are reset.</p>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </div>
