<section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl" data-sw-animation="fade-up">
    <p class="ws-index ws-ink">Reference</p>
    <h2 class="ws-display mt-3 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl" data-sw-text="ref_title">Every attribute.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100">
    <table class="table">
      <thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap font-code text-sm">data-effect</td><td><code class="font-code text-sm">fade</code> (default) or <code class="font-code text-sm">slide</code>. Multi-item rows need <code class="font-code text-sm">slide</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap font-code text-sm">data-loop</td><td>Looping is on by default. <code class="font-code text-sm">false</code> stops at the ends and dims the arrow there.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap font-code text-sm">data-autoplay · data-interval</td><td>Advance in steps, every N ms (default 5000). Pauses on hover and focus.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap font-code text-sm">data-autoscroll · data-autoscroll-speed</td><td>A continuous ticker instead of steps, in px per frame (default 2).</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap font-code text-sm">data-wheel</td><td>Mouse wheel and trackpad gestures move the slides.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap font-code text-sm">data-autoheight</td><td>Animates the height to the slide in view. Needs the slide effect.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap font-code text-sm">data-item-align</td><td><code class="font-code text-sm">center</code> (default), <code class="font-code text-sm">start</code> or <code class="font-code text-sm">end</code>, for scrolling and for a row with fewer slides than it fits.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap font-code text-sm">data-arrows</td><td><code class="font-code text-sm">edge</code> or <code class="font-code text-sm">circle</code>. By default a single-slide carousel gets edge arrows and a multi-item row gets circles.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap font-code text-sm">data-click-next</td><td>A click on a slide advances it. On by default for the single-slide edge style.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap font-code text-sm">data-kenburns</td><td>The hero look: the active slide's <code class="font-code text-sm">.sw-kenburns</code> layer pans and zooms, and its <code class="font-code text-sm">.sw-caption</code> rises in.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap font-code text-sm">--sw-items</td><td>Slides per view, as a CSS variable on the root. Fractions leave a peek.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

